It's interesting how idiosyncratic people's browsing techniques are.
My tendencies follow two distinct patterns:

1. I go to the website and use a search function to find what I want (note: for websites built on a single
page, that manifests itself by doing a wordsearch within the browser)

2. I take advantage of any "directory structure" that the website has to push/aid me toward what I'm looking
for (and perhaps find the critical key word that I can use for a search).

The Wiki, for me, seems to perform better than the single page on both accounts. 

But the biggest advantage of the Wiki, for me, is that is radically simplifies sharing and
does so in a fashion that allows one to have a lots of "tricks" (math syntax, syntax highlighting,
command hyperlinks,  figures, ...)

Just my $.02

Damian


